course: dictionary
lesson: 6061
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word mercury is a good example. «Mercury is hard to spot because it never strays far from the Sun» is about a planet, because it is seen low in the sky near the Sun.
explain: The same word can name something very different. «Mercury is the only metal that is liquid at room temperature» is about a silvery metal. The capital M is a clue too: Mercury the planet and Mercury the god have a capital letter, but mercury the metal does not.
explain: Read the words around the word. «The mercury is rising» means the temperature is going up, so here mercury means the level of heat, not a metal or a planet. Ask: which meaning makes sense in this sentence? Then test your choice by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: Mercury the planet is the closest planet to the Sun and the smallest planet in our Solar System.
fact: «Mercury goes around in 88 days», so its year is much shorter than ours.
fact: Mercury the metal is a silvery liquid at room temperature, and it is poisonous.
fact: «A broken mercury thermometer is a job for a grown-up.» Never touch the silver drops; tell an adult.
fact: Mercury was the Roman messenger god, shown with wings on his sandals.
exercise: «Mercury goes around the Sun in 88 days.» What does Mercury mean here? | A Roman messenger god with wings on his sandals | *A planet, the closest one to the Sun | A silvery metal in an old thermometer | A small grey cloud
exercise: «The mercury is rising, so the day is getting warmer.» What does mercury mean here? | A silver liquid in a tube | A messenger from the gods | Tiny craters on a planet | *The temperature going up
exercise: «Mercury is poisonous, so a broken thermometer is a job for a grown-up.» What does poisonous mean? | Very hot | *Harmful if you eat it or touch it | Shiny and bright | Fast-moving
test: «Mercury is the only metal that is liquid at room temperature.» Which word tells you Mercury means the metal? | liquid | room | *metal | only
test: «Venus, not Mercury, is the hottest planet.» What does Mercury mean here? | A Roman messenger god | *A planet, the one closest to the Sun | The temperature going up | A silvery metal used in thermometers
exam: «The god Mercury ran with wings on his sandals.» Which meaning of mercury is this? | *A Roman messenger god | A silvery metal | A planet near the Sun | The temperature going up
